what:
Goal of Anvil, stated by the user: guarantee code quality so it scales with minimal or no slop; token and time savings are secondary.

Shipped while Claude Code worked on the project (all pushed to origin/main):
- Tier 1 guards: overengineering:unused-new-code and duplication:new-code (both blocking ERRORs).
- anvil review log and a Quality section in anvil stats (escape rate per category).
- Stop and hook messages that are plain and localized. Language comes from config.language, then ANVIL_LANG, then the Claude settings language, then the OS locale.
- Orchestrator mode with parallel executors:
  - per-executor SCOPE read from the executor's own transcript;
  - overlapping scopes refused;
  - anvil check --scope.
- Lean executor (Claude Code): a tools allowlist cut the first prompt from 58k to about 18.5k tokens. `anvil orchestrator tools` picks which MCP servers executors load (orchestrator.executor_tools).
- Formatting and gates:
  - rustfmt.toml with use_small_heuristics="Max"; the workspace is fmt-clean and CI runs cargo fmt --check;
  - the .git/hooks/pre-commit hook (anvil check --staged --tier 0) is installed in this repo.
- Slop benchmark in crates/anvil-cli/slop_bench/*.case, run by tests/slop_bench.rs:
  - 43 cases;
  - it fails on any missed or unexpected finding, or when a known-gap starts being reported;
  - `cargo test -p anvil-cli --test slop_bench -- --nocapture` prints the per-rule table.
- Mandatory review in orchestrator mode:
  - `anvil review packet` and `anvil review approve`, also as MCP review_packet and review_approve;
  - task_done is refused until the current content fingerprint is approved;
  - executors cannot approve.
- Fix: test-tampering checks now see untracked files via git::pending_diffs.
- New rule no-swallowed-errors (TS/JS, PHP, Kotlin, Dart, Python, Rust), reported only on newly added lines (NEW_CODE_ONLY_RULES).
